          "question": {
            "text": "Which of the following order is not correct?",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "pdB5X",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{MeBr}>\\mathrm{Me}_{2} \\mathrm{CHBr}>\\mathrm{Me}_{3} \\mathrm{CBr}>$\n$\\mathrm{Et}_{3} \\mathrm{CBr}\\left(\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2\\right)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "sf0yF",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{Me}_{3} \\mathrm{CBr}>\\mathrm{Me}_{2} \\mathrm{CHBr}>\\mathrm{Me}_{2} \\mathrm{CH.CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Br}>$\n$\\mathrm{MeCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{Br} .\\left(\\mathrm{E}_{2}\\right)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "l5cMH",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{PhCH}_{2} \\mathrm{Br}>\\mathrm{Ph} \\mathrm{CHBrMe}>\\mathrm{PhCBrMe}_{2}>$\n$\\operatorname{PhCBrMePh}\\left(\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1\\right)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "WPDXV",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{MeI}>\\mathrm{MeBr}>\\mathrm{MeCl}>\\mathrm{MeF}\\left(\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2\\right)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The more is the stability of intermediate carbonium ion, the more is the chance of $\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 1$ mechanism. The intermediates obtained will be \n$\\mathrm{Ph}^{+} \\mathrm{C} \\mathrm{H}_{2}(\\mathrm{i}), \\mathrm{Ph} \\mathrm{C} \\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Me}(\\mathrm{ii})$\n$\\mathrm{Ph} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Me}_{2}\\left(\\right.$ iii) $, \\mathrm{Ph} \\mathrm{C}^{+} \\mathrm{MePh}$ (iv)\nThe stabilty is of the order iv $>\\mathrm{iii}>\\mathrm{ii}>\\mathrm{i}$",
            "image": null
          },
