          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "<p>Identify compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math> in the following reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mrow></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>Fe</mi></mrow></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>HCl</mi></mrow></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math></p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "YB36l",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></math>-bromotoluene",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "X7Nv8",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>-bromotoluene",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "26dP6",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>-bromotoluene",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "mZa7D",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-bromo, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math> trichlorotoluene",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>Side chain hydrogen atoms are substituted by halogens in presence of light or heat by free radical mechanism. Ring hydrogens are substituted in presence of Lewis acid by electrofile. Alkyl halide (R-X) are reduced by Zn/HCl into alkane.</p><p>The degree of unsaturation for compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math> is three&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math>, as it reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math> is toluene, i.e <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The whole reaction occurs as follows:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/b5ccc3ad-260d-4c39-98bf-fbb659318bee-image.png\" style=\"width: 742px; height: 198px;\" /></p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
