        {
          "_id": "64c0e8086f5bfc7ab78ae9fb",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7d",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2019-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2019",
              "title": "BITSAT 2019"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "<p>In the reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></mfenced></math> are respectively.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/e84e7933-f335-46c9-ba6c-e10d6c38ff10-4c85ae67-614f-4990-a868-28821819c8d3-image.png\" style=\"width: 677px; height: 163px;\" /></p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "apGjb",
              "text": "<img height=\"179\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/58825c06-434a-4693-9333-1ad3c3914bbf-image.png\" width=\"272\" />",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "uEbdi",
              "text": "<img height=\"169\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/e7f0f7d7-c00b-497a-877e-356e49cbfc65-image.png\" width=\"254\" />",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "euOIF",
              "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/c2536ab8-2613-42a3-9a44-8968003c8c45-image.png\" style=\"width: 317px; height: 168px;\" />",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "vKFh4",
              "text": "<img height=\"164\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/fbd04f9f-f710-432d-ac26-a479fd2d4dce-image.png\" width=\"343\" />",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>The given reaction is for preparation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DDT</mi></math> (dichlorodiphenyl trichloroethane). Complete reaction is given as follows.</p><p>(i)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/c49419d1-5434-42c7-b515-e22645f3c73a-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 130px;\" /></p><p>(ii)&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/230d6a1e-e8e5-4e0d-9c43-c0793d7fc9ca-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 97px;\" /></p><p>Dichloro-diphenyl-trichloroethane (DDT) is prepared by heating chloral and chlorobenzene in 1:2 ratio in the presence of conc. sulphuric acid.</p><p>DDT is used as an insecticide. It is also used as a mosquito repellant.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
