        {
          "_id": "64c0e7ed6f5bfc7ab78ae912",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7b",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2017-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2017",
              "title": "BITSAT 2017"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Chlorobenzene</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Reaction</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mover><mi>Phenol</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Reaction</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mover><mi>Salicylaldehyde</mi></math>.</p><p>The reactions(s) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><none></none><mo>&#39;</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>&#39;</mo></mmultiscripts></math> and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><none></none><mo>&#39;</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>&#39;</mo></mmultiscripts></math> respectively are</p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "7Sm9G",
              "text": "Fries rearrangement and Kolbe",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Upk0j",
              "text": "Cumene and Reimer-Tiemann",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "SpD9l",
              "text": "Dow and Reimer-Tiemann",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Hydca",
              "text": "Dow and Sandmeyer.",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>Phenol is manufactured by heating chlorobenzene with 10% aqueous NaOH solution at about 623K under 300 atm and in the presence of copper salt acting as a catalyst to form sodium phenoxide. The sodium salt when treated with dil. HCl, gives phenol. This method is known as Dow&#39;s process.&nbsp;</p><p>When phenol is heated with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in the presence of aqueous&nbsp;NaOH, an aldehydic group&nbsp;(&minus;CHO)&nbsp;get introduced in the ring at a position ortho to the phenolic group. This reaction is known as the Reimer-Tiemann reaction.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/6d6bb09a-1ad7-45bc-911a-55f8587d5688-image.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 163px;\" /></p>",
            "image": null
          },
